{
  "$comment": "Catalogue of Google MCP servers. NOT active configuration — /google:mcp reads this and writes chosen entries into the PROJECT's .mcp.json. No credentials here, ever: env values are variable names the user supplies. toolCount/schemaBytes were measured, not estimated; see measuredAt.",
  "version": 1,
  "measuredAt": "2026-08-05",
  "notes": {
    "remoteAuth": "Every *.googleapis.com/mcp endpoint answers initialize and tools/list WITHOUT credentials, so it connects, dumps its whole tool schema into the session, and only fails when a tool is actually called. accounts.google.com exposes no registration_endpoint, so Dynamic Client Registration is impossible and Claude Code cannot self-register: pass your own OAuth client with `claude mcp add --client-id <id> --client-secret --callback-port <port>`. Run /google:setup for the walkthrough.",
    "cost": "Measured 2026-08-05. Enabling every verified remote server at once would cost roughly 5.7 MB of JSON schema in every session. chronicle alone is 3.7 MB. Enable per project, never globally.",
    "status": "verified = probed, with toolCount/schemaBytes/measuredAt. listed = taken from Google's supported-products page but never probed; /google:mcp add refuses these. unavailable = probed and found not to exist.",
    "gws": "The Google Workspace CLI removed its `gws mcp` subcommand in 0.8.0 — a Discovery-API-wide MCP server exposed 200-400 tools. The gws-* skills in this plugin replace it at a fraction of the context cost."
  },
  "servers": {
